<title>USA: Paracelsian files patent application.</title>
<headline>Paracelsian files patent application.</headline>
<dateline>ITHACA, N.Y. 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Paracelsian Inc said Monday that it has filed a patent application with the U.S. Patent Trademarks Office relating to ways of inhibiting CD4+T cell depletion induced by HIV-1 infected cells.</p>
<p>The company said its scientists have discovered methods of protecting CD4+T cells which may be useful with antiviral therapeutics to prevent their loss.</p>
<p>HIV infection eventually produces the loss of CD4+T cells, resulting in the onset of AIDS.</p>
</text>
